# Project Structure

This repo has two apps at the root (see `README.md` and `docs/phases/`):

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `server/` | NestJS backend (API on port 4000, `/api` prefix) |
| `client/` | Next.js frontend (port 3000) |
| `server/src/common/` | Cross-cutting NestJS code (guards, pipes, filters, interceptors, middleware) |
| `server/src/database/` | TypeORM config, migrations |
| `client/src/types/` | Frontend TypeScript interfaces |
| `ai-agents/` | AI agent pipeline (analyzer, refactorer, orchestrator, etc.) |
| `docs/phases/` | Phase-by-phase implementation docs |

There is **no** `apps/api`, `apps/web`, or `packages/` workspace today. Use `server/` and `client/` paths in all code and docs.

## Docker

Root `docker-compose.yml` defines services **`server`** and **`client`**. After structural changes, verify with:

```bash
docker-compose up --build -d
docker-compose exec server npm run migration:run:prod   # if schema changed
```

## NestJS feature modules

Organize by **feature/domain**, not by layer. Feature folders live directly under `server/src/`:

```
server/src/meetings/
├── meetings.controller.ts
├── meetings.service.ts
├── meetings.module.ts
├── dto/
├── entities/
├── interfaces/    # response shapes when needed
└── enums/         # domain enums when needed
```

Existing features include `meetings/`, `transcriptions/`, `summaries/`, `auth/`, `storage/`, `extraction/`, `organizations/`, `organization-users/`, `health/`, and `ai-agents/`.

## Enums

- Domain literals used more than once (roles, statuses, error codes, integration auth types) belong in `enums/*.enum.ts` on the server and mirrored in `client/src/types/` on the client.
- Prefer string enums whose values match the API/DB. Do not introduce a second parallel set of string constants for the same concept.

## Layer responsibilities

- **Controllers** — routing and request validation only. No business logic.
- **Services** — business logic. One responsibility per service; split when a service does more than one job.
- **Shared API contracts** — server shapes in `dto/` and `interfaces/`; client shapes in `client/src/types/`. Do not duplicate or drift; keep field names and enum values aligned.
- **AuthZ** — enforce on the server; client role gates are navigation/UX only. See `docs/architecture/access-control.md` and `docs/architecture/security.md`.
